SECURITY REVIEW
- All 37 individual baseline production advisory objects are patched; no waiver.
- Next actually loads sharp 0.35.5, libvips 8.18.7, libheif 1.23.5, librsvg 2.63.2,
  and its CSS-loader resolution is PostCSS 8.5.23. No image-package override.
- Benign AVIF/PNG optimize over actual Next HTTP; SVG, malformed bytes and remote URL
  are refused; actual consumer/terminal OG PNG dimensions verified; unavailable
  dynamic OG is 503/no-store/Retry-After 60 and extra image parameters return 400.
- PostCSS baseline 8.4.31 negative control: missing-from map reads generated
  SYNTHETIC_NON_SECRET_MAP_SENTINEL_114. Patched 8.5.23 denies it and traversal;
  legitimate adjacent maps remain usable. No secret or real sensitive file used.
- Real PostgreSQL/TLS tests below cover concurrency, transactional rollback,
  quotas, leases, monotonic fencing, restart persistence, outage fail-closed,
  SCRAM privilege boundaries, certificate/hostname failures, deadlines, redaction.
- No app/lib/data/public-existing/experiments/scheduler/workflow changes. Original
  activation pins remain PRODUCTION_RPC_ENABLED=false and LIVE_APPROVAL enabled=false,
  storeHost=null, vercelProjectId=null. No credentials read/provisioned or live RPC.
- Focused changed-text secret-pattern scan: no matches; no values printed.
- Full developer audit residuals require owner review; no claims about deployed
  host security, physical mobile devices or provider permissions/activation.

DEVELOPMENT CORRECTION (resolved, not counted as passing)
An earlier extended browser run had 3 test-selector failures: the metric container
included the hidden accessible term along with its value. The assertion now targets
its dd. The final fresh-process run below passes all 81 cases. Initial local runner
setup/lint issues were corrected before these final command results.


